  "statement": "A prime number \\(p\\) is mundane if there exist positive integers \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) less than \\(\\frac{p}{2}\\) such that \\(\\frac{a b-1}{p}\\) is a positive integer. Find, with proof, all prime numbers that are not mundane.",
